{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Rat","lean:module:QOU.Mass.CarrierCrossingQuantisation"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.no_uniform_bond_model_reproduces_b3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.no_uniform_bond_model_reproduces_b3","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L267-L275","doc":"**So no uniform pairwise-bond model reproduces the AME `b₃/b₂`.** The\nmeasured value is strictly positive; every such model is `≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.bondAdditive_nonpositive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.bondAdditive_nonpositive","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L257-L265","doc":"**Every uniform pairwise-bond model gives a non-positive `b₃`.** The bond\ncount on three nucleons cannot exceed `C(3,2) = 3`, and the inversion subtracts\nthree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.bRatioOfBondCounts_allPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.bRatioOfBondCounts_allPairs","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L253-L255","doc":"All-pairs is the `n(3) = 3` row — exactly zero, and still not positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.bRatioOfBondCounts_chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.bRatioOfBondCounts_chain","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L249-L251","doc":"The chain is the `n(3) = 2` row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.bRatioOfBondCounts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.bRatioOfBondCounts","kind":"def","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L245-L247","doc":"`b₃/b₂` for a bond-additive model with uniform bond value, as a function of\nthe bond counts alone — the bond value cancels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainAdditive_b3_never_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainAdditive_b3_never_positive","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L212-L222","doc":"**So a chain-additive model can never produce a positive `b₃`.** Asking it for\none is asking the wrong object — which is the reframing, and the reason this is a\nquestion about the comparison rather than about the physics. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainAdditive_bRatio_eq_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainAdditive_bRatio_eq_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L205-L210","doc":"**Hence `b₃/b₂ = -1` for every chain-additive model.** This is what the three\nbond-additive channels were measuring; it is an identity, not three findings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainAdditive_b3_eq_neg_b2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainAdditive_b3_eq_neg_b2","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L196-L202","doc":"**The Ursell three-body cumulant of a chain-additive model is `-b₂`,\nidentically.** `B(3) - 3B(2) = 2b - 3b = -b`. No choice of bond value, weighting\nor scale changes it — the `-1` is the inversion's three pair terms meeting the\nchain's two bonds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainBinding_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainBinding_three","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L191-L193","doc":"`A = 3`: two bonds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainBinding_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainBinding_two","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L186-L188","doc":"The deuteron: one bond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainBinding","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L181-L183","doc":"Binding of a chain of `A` nucleons that is additive over bonds with a uniform\nbond value `b`: one term per bond, and a chain has `A - 1` of them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.counts_diverge_at_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.counts_diverge_at_four","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L176-L177","doc":"The divergence is not a small-`A` accident: it widens. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.pair_deficit_at_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.pair_deficit_at_three","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L172-L174","doc":"**And diverge at `A = 3`, by exactly one pair.** That single missing pair is\nthe whole of the `-b₂` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.counts_agree_at_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.counts_agree_at_two","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L169-L170","doc":"**They agree at `A = 2`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainBondCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.chainBondCount","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L165-L167","doc":"Bonds in a chain on `A` nucleons — what the forced layout supplies\n(`QOU.Mass.StrandLayoutForcesChain`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.pairCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UrsellChainMismatch.pairCount","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UrsellChainMismatch.lean#L162-L163","doc":"Pairs among `A` objects — what the Ursell inversion charges for. ","signatureChunk":0}]}